# ============================================================================
# General Build/Test Artifacts
# ============================================================================
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak*

# ============================================================================
# 1stcontact site framework (see DOC-12)
# ============================================================================
# Rendered site output — derived, regenerated by `1c render` / `1c publish`.
# Never committed (also matched by the bare `dist/` above; kept explicit here).
/storage/dist/
# Sandbox: throwaway test sites for experimenting with site creation. Never committed.
# Real sites live under storage/sites/ and ARE tracked.
/storage/sandbox/
# Reference captures (DOC-13 §2.10) — third-party page bundles from `1c capture`.
# Gitignored: uncommitted third-party material, self-contained for offline re-map.
/storage/references/
# Scratch space: repro working files (values-diff JSON, aligned crops). Never committed.
/storage/tmp/
# Draft change journals (REQ-131) — one per site, beside the site it describes.
# Every copy edit appends a record, so tracking these would churn the tree on
# every keystroke-settle; and nothing depends on them surviving a clone, because
# a missing journal degrades a reader to a full re-read rather than to a wrong
# answer.
/storage/sites/*/.journal.json
# Assistant transcripts (REQ-122) — one persisted conversation per site, written
# by the builder's AI host. Operator-local and often verbatim business detail;
# never committed.
/storage/chat/

# ============================================================================
# System knowledge base (REQ-123)
# ============================================================================
# The corpus and its indexes are DERIVED — `1c kb build` exports every doc
# ticket, embeds it, and generates the awareness map. Ignored on three grounds:
# the documents' source of truth is the ticket store, which IS tracked, so a
# committed copy would be a second one to drift; the embeddings are binary and
# would churn the tree on every rebuild; and the map is regenerated whenever the
# documents move. The DECLARATION (kb/knowledge_bases.json) is authored data,
# not derived, and is tracked.
/kb/system/

# ============================================================================
# Cloudflare Wrangler / Miniflare
# ============================================================================
# Local dev + build cache (miniflare state, deploy bundles). Regenerated by
# `wrangler dev` / `wrangler deploy [--dry-run]`. Never committed.
.wrangler/

# REQ-145 — the control app's build output, both halves. Built by `1c assets`
# from the builder client and the out-of-repo shared component store.
#
# `src/generated/importmap.json` is generated too, and is ignored for a REASON
# the repo already enforces: a checked-in copy of a generator's output is a
# SECOND DEFINITION SITE for the component scope, and BUG-32's scan fails on it
# (an `index.html` was deleted for exactly this before). `bin/build` runs
# `1c assets` before it typechecks, so the Worker always has one to import.
/apps/control-app/dist-assets/
/apps/control-app/src/generated/
